    "result_text": "Done. The build is green.\n\nI implemented the level-4 tenure rule with minimal structural impact \u2014 a single-file change confined to `MembershipLevel`:\n\n- The three pre-tenure factors (base 1, +1 email, +1 zero-namesake) are still capped at 3 via `Math.min(level, 3)`.\n- A new factor adds `+1` when tenure exceeds 365 days, computed from `registrationDate`.\n- A small private nested `Tenure` helper isolates the day calculation (and null-safety), keeping the `of` method itself simple and its surrounding class complexity low.\n\nBecause a newly created owner has zero tenure (its `registrationDate` is today, or null), the tenure factor never fires at creation, so a new owner with an email and `namesakeCount` of 0 lands at level 3 \u2014 exactly what `coreNewOwnerCappedAtLevel3` asserts.",
